Cesium is designed for mathematical computing and linear algebra. It puts performance, explicit memory management and mathematical expressiveness first, and stays compatible with the C ABI.

Its design draws most on C, Zig and MATLAB. The name is the element of the atomic clock: a language whose first aim is speed at run time shares a name with what defines the second.
